    "video": {
      "name": "Keto Burrito Bowl [Beefy & Super Easy]",
      "description": "This beefy burrito bowl skillet is the next best thing to tasty, filling nachos on the keto diet. The best thing about this recipe, besides how delicious it is, that everything cooks in one pan so after dinner cleanup is minimal.\n\nThe cheesy beef and cauliflower rice mixtures pairs up deliciously with all the fresh vegetables such as avocados, limes, jalapenos, and tomatoes! To save some time, use pre-made cauliflower rice and pre-shredded cheese.\n\nRead the full recipe with full nutrition breakdown and step-by-step pictures over at:\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nIngredients:\nBeefy Bowl:\n16 ounce ground beef\n3 tablespoon olive oil, divided\n1/2 medium yellow onion, minced\n600 gram cauliflower rice\n1 teaspoon garlic powder\n1 teaspoon onion powder\n1 teaspoon paprika\n1/2 teaspoon chili powder\n1 teaspoon cumin\n1/4 cup beef broth\n12 ounce canned tomatoes with green chiles, drained\n2 cup shredded monterey jack cheese\nSalt and pepper to taste\n\nGarnish:\n1/2 medium red bell pepper, diced\n1 medium jalapeno pepper\n1 medium avocado, diced\n1/4 medium red onion, minced\n1/4 cup fresh cilantro, chopped\n1 medium lime, sliced\n\nNutrition Summary: This makes a total of 4 servings of Keto Beefy Burrito Bowl. Each serving comes out to be 762 calories, 59.3g fat, 13.6g net carbs, and 40.2g protein.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSee more keto recipes, knowledge and tips on the website to keep your weight loss going strong.\n\nEverything you need to know about the keto diet:\n\nGetting started? Everything you need is here:\n\nWe also make things easy with this 14 day diet plan:\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nFollow Ruled.Me for more tasty food:",
